    * parameters: ('- **Strategic Differentiation (The Unfair Advantage):** \n  - Positioning the brand in the Mid-to-High Artisanal Sweet Spot (EGP 600–850) as "Affordable Luxury."\n  - Using heavy-duty, heat-resistant, multi-cycle upcycled glass containers designed to convert into kitchen storage jars, coffee mugs, or plant holders after the candle burns out.\n  - 100% pure soy wax with treated cotton wicks (clean-burning, toxin-free promise).\n  - Narrative Scent Architecture inspired by local and regional heritage with a modern twist.\n  - Gift-ready luxury unboxing experience (cloth/thick paper packaging, scented cards, handwritten notes) to drive organic User-Generated Content (UGC).\n- **High-Impact Launch Campaign Strategy (Total Budget: EGP 100,000):**\n  - **Phase 1: Teaser & Hype (Week 1):** Allocate EGP 20,000 to build curiosity, gather waitlist leads, and run cinematic BTS (Behind-The-Scenes) / ASMR pouring Reels.\n  - **Phase 2: Launch & Direct Conversion (Weeks 2-3):** Allocate EGP 50,000 for aggressive sales, highlighting the upcycled glass value proposition and clean-burning benefits against imported alternatives.\n  - **Phase 3: Retargeting & Scaling (Week 4):** Allocate EGP 30,000 to retarget high-intent engagers with social proof, customer reviews, and bundled offers.\n- **Audience Targeting Parameters:** Ages 24–45, residing in New Cairo, 5th Settlement, Sheikh Zayed, 6th of October, Maadi, Zamalek, and Smouha. Interests: Home decor, interior design, soy candles, aromatherapy, self-care, wellness, and sustainable living.\n- **Future Growth Vectors:** Expanding into B2B hospitality (private-label candles for boutique hotels and spas) and quarterly sensory subscription boxes.', {'active_plans': '- **Strategic Differentiation (The Unfair Advantage):** \n  - Positioning the brand in the Mid-to-High Artisanal Sweet Spot (EGP 600–850) as "Affordable Luxury."\n  - Using heavy-duty, heat-resistant, multi-cycle upcycled glass containers designed to convert into kitchen storage jars, coffee mugs, or plant holders after the candle burns out.\n  - 100% pure soy wax with treated cotton wicks (clean-burning, toxin-free promise).\n  - Narrative Scent Architecture inspired by local and regional heritage with a modern twist.\n  - Gift-ready luxury unboxing experience (cloth/thick paper packaging, scented cards, handwritten notes) to drive organic User-Generated Content (UGC).\n- **High-Impact Launch Campaign Strategy (Total Budget: EGP 100,000):**\n  - **Phase 1: Teaser & Hype (Week 1):** Allocate EGP 20,000 to build curiosity, gather waitlist leads, and run cinematic BTS (Behind-The-Scenes) / ASMR pouring Reels.\n  - **Phase 2: Launch & Direct Conversion (Weeks 2-3):** Allocate EGP 50,000 for aggressive sales, highlighting the upcycled glass value proposition and clean-burning benefits against imported alternatives.\n  - **Phase 3: Retargeting & Scaling (Week 4):** Allocate EGP 30,000 to retarget high-intent engagers with social proof, customer reviews, and bundled offers.\n- **Audience Targeting Parameters:** Ages 24–45, residing in New Cairo, 5th Settlement, Sheikh Zayed, 6th of October, Maadi, Zamalek, and Smouha. Interests: Home decor, interior design, soy candles, aromatherapy, self-care, wellness, and sustainable living.\n- **Future Growth Vectors:** Expanding into B2B hospitality (private-label candles for boutique hotels and spas) and quarterly sensory subscription boxes.', 'source': 'ltm_compressor', 'created_at': '2026-10-11T20:11:09.435131+00:00', 'updated_at': '2026-10-12T10:53:38.167323+00:00'}, 'mem_plan_ba3c879d057b')
